    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0108" n="34" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg34"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/13451</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-21T12:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 21, 1917, noon</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 7.15 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6056. Admiral Sims says: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Situation here is critical, serious, and daily growing worse. During last
                            24 hours, 13 ships, 44,000 tons lost, not counting 4 mine sweepers,
                            mostly southwest of Ireland. April 1 to 18, inclusive, 408,000 tons
                            sunk. Of utmost urgency that we give maximum assistance immediately,
                            every other consideration should be subordinated. I urge the immediate
                            sailing of all available destroyers <pb facs="0109" n="35" xml:id="pg35"
                            /> followed at earliest possible moment by reenforcement of destroyers
                            and all light-draft craft available. Fuel is available on this side.
                            Vitally important that this information be treated with utmost secrecy
                            and urgency.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
